  "notes": [
    "v3 = v2 pipeline with TWO OUTCOME-DEFINITION FIXES. The cohort FUNNEL is UNCHANGED from v2 (same 7 pre-decision STROBE steps, same exclusions): analytic N (cohort_primary==1) = 239,736; CSV rows = 291,766. No exclusion step was touched.",
    "v3 PRE-DECISION cohort: HC-inclusion filter DROPPED (CONTRACTS \u00a79-A); hemorrhage control is an OUTCOME component of major_hemorrhage_event, not a cohort filter. STROBE funnel = 7 pre-decision steps.",
    "Both QC gates FAIL on the COMPILED export: all 33 of its date/time columns are 0% filled, so no death DATETIME is derivable there. That does NOT mean time-to-death is unavailable -- see the finaldischarge_days block: the RAW PUF carries day-resolution arrival-anchored offsets, and the <=48h restriction IS built. The gates are retained unchanged as an honest statement about the compiled export only.",
    "v3 W1 FULL COMPLIANCE (supersedes the plan's 'rebut the <=48h half' posture, which was based on a false premise): FINALDISCHARGEDAYS ('Time from ED/Hospital Arrival to Final Discharge (days)') is joined from the RAW PUF_TRAUMA.csv files on inc_key. It is ALREADY arrival-anchored and is used DIRECTLY -- it must NOT be differenced against HOSPITALARRIVALDAYS, which is incident-anchored (that subtraction manufactures impossible negative values). Evidence: logs/timing_evidence_v3.md.",
    "TIMING CUT IS ON HOURS. FINALDISCHARGEHRS (elapsed hours, two decimals, arrival-anchored, ~98.8% raw fill) exists in all six raw years and gives W1's '<=48h' EXACTLY. An earlier build used 'finaldischarge_days <= 2' and asserted that AY 2019-2024 has no minute/hour fields -- that assertion was FALSE and is withdrawn. The header search had been widened from *_DATE/*_TIME to *DAYS but never to *HRS. The raw files also carry HOSPITALARRIVALHRS, EDDISCHARGEHRS, INPATIENTHRS, ANGIOGRAPHYHRS, HMRRHGCTRLSURGHRS, TRAUMASURGEONARRIVALHRS.",
    "The calendar-day rule is SUPERSEDED but retained as death_hemorrhagic_dayrule / death_le48h_dayrule. finaldischarge_days is a calendar-day INDEX, not elapsed time: day 3 straddles 48h. The day rule had 0 false positives (100% specific) but MISSED 633 deaths that truly occurred within 48h.",
    "MISSING-VALUE RULE (explicit): a missing finaldischarge_hrs is treated as NOT within 48h, so such a death does NOT enter death_le48h or death_hemorrhagic. Conservative -- it shrinks the primary outcome. Deaths excluded by missingness ALONE = 287 (of 429 deaths with no hours value). The rule is BOUNDED, not assumed, by the retained column death_hemorrhagic_missing_incl.",
    "DIFFERENTIAL ASCERTAINMENT (for script 12): timing-field missingness among deaths is 4.395% in the derivation window (2019-2022) vs 0.803% in validation (2023-2024) -- a +3.592 pp gap sitting exactly on the temporal split. Because missing timing is scored as NOT within 48h, death_hemorrhagic is under-counted more in derivation. 12 must report this as a DATA-COLLECTION ARTIFACT, not as model miscalibration.",
    "AIS PARSER DEFECT FIX (inherited from v2, corrected in v3): the compiled AIS export stores AISPreDot as a FLOAT, so chapter-0 codes like '010008' round-trip to '10008' and the region digit read from position 0 was the SECOND digit -- scoring External/chapter-0 codes as HEAD (or CHEST) injuries. Fixed with .str.zfill(6) before the region digit is taken. Nationally 12,898 of 25,483,291 AIS rows are 5-digit; 7,026 were mis-mapped to region 1 (head) and 192 to region 4 (chest). Direction is INFLATION-ONLY. ais_head is outcome-defining in v3 (death_hemorrhagic), so this is a corrected OUTCOME misclassification and must be registered as a deviation from the v2 SAP. The AIS-6 exclusion is region-independent, so the cohort funnel is unaffected.",
    "FIX 1 (S1) unit-aware transfusion decoder: TQIP_HC_BLOOD_UNIT is 100% blank and TQIP_HC_BLOOD_4HR is bimodal (units cluster 1-100, mL cluster >=200, near-empty 101-199 gap). substantial_transfusion = (blood_4h >= 1000) | (4 <= blood_4h <= 100). The v2 mL-only rule is retained as substantial_transfusion_ml_only (named sensitivity, and a strict subset of the new rule). blood_4h_scale records the inferred scale per row. blood_4h NaN -> not flagged (downstream sensitivity).",
    "FIX 1 delta: substantial_transfusion 14,238 (v2 mL-only) -> 17,156 (v3 unit-aware); 2,918 newly flagged, all from the 4-100 units band. 2,957 records at 1-3 U are below the >=4 U threshold and are NOT flagged. 11 records sit in the 101-199 ambiguous gap and 0 of them are flagged. See logs/fix1_transfusion_audit.md.",
    "mtp_equivalent is DEFINITIONALLY IDENTICAL to the v3 substantial_transfusion (>=4 U or >=1000 mL / 4 h; PMID 25440492). It is a separate column only because script 17 analyses it as a standalone secondary outcome -- it is NOT an independent endpoint.",
    "FIX 2 (W1, FULL) hemorrhagic-death component: death_hemorrhagic = death_inhosp & (ais_head < 4) & (finaldischarge_hrs <= 48) is the PRIMARY composite death component AND the mortality-only anchor. The timing cut is on HOURS (exact); the calendar-day rule is SUPERSEDED and kept only as a sensitivity. Retained named sensitivities: death_hemorrhagic_headais (head-AIS half only), death_le48h (timing half only), death_hemorrhagic_dayrule / death_le48h_dayrule (superseded day proxy), death_hemorrhagic_dayfallback and death_hemorrhagic_edincl (pre-specified partial recovery of untimed deaths), death_hemorrhagic_missing_incl (upper bound), death_inhosp (all-cause), death_ed (ED_DISPOSITION_CODE=='MOR').",
    "FIX 2 ladder: death_inhosp 13,426 -> & ais_head<4 8,501 -> & <=48h 4,191. Other ordering: 13,426 -> & <=48h 6,408 -> & ais_head<4 4,191. Untimed-death recovery rungs: primary 4,191 / day-fallback 4,209 / ED-inclusive 4,253 / all-missing-included 4,478. Superseded day-rule proxy 3,884. death_ed = 1,818. See logs/fix2_death_audit.md.",
    "v3 PRIMARY composite = received_hc | death_hemorrhagic | substantial_transfusion. Co-primary anti-circularity = patient_state_composite (death_hemorrhagic | substantial_transfusion; HC dropped). Mortality-only anchor is now death_hemorrhagic (head AIS < 4 AND <=48h). Retained composites: major_hemorrhage_event_headais (n = 29,096, the head-AIS-half-only variant) and the exact v2 primary major_hemorrhage_event_v2def (n = 31,054, fork-fidelity gate).",
    "cc_anticoag (preexisting code 31) and cc_bleeding (code 4) are NOT Charlson components -- collected separately in build_charlson; charlson unaffected. unstable_ring = ICD S32.81* (disrupted ring).",
    "sbp_unrecordable = raw SBP2==0 sentinel captured BEFORE the 0->NaN mask (MNAR-as-signal); it is a subset of sbp2-missing.",
    "blood_4h fill (primary pre-decision cohort) = 91.812%.",
    "FIX 7 companion fields plasma_4h (TQIP_HC_PLASMA_4HR) and platelet_4h (TQIP_HC_PLATE_4HR) are now pulled into the cohort CSV for the EXPLORATORY balanced-resuscitation subgroup. NO decoder is applied to them -- they are raw-numeric and NaN-preserving. Fill: plasma_4h = 80.678%, platelet_4h = 80.682% (plan expected ~27.3%). Their unit-vs-mL band distributions and a data-driven bimodality verdict are in logs/fix1_transfusion_audit.md \u00a76; any ratio built from them inherits an undetermined scale and must be labelled exploratory.",
    "FORK-FIDELITY GATE (CONTRACTS \u00a73.1 / \u00a713 G2e-G2f): every carried-forward v2 figure (CSV rows, analytic N, cc_anticoag, cc_bleeding, unstable_ring, sbp_unrecordable, received_hc, death_inhosp, substantial_transfusion_ml_only, major_hemorrhage_event_v2def + its rate, v2-definition patient_state_composite, full-CSV blood_4h 1-50 band) is recomputed and checked -- result: PASS. See the 'fork_fidelity' block above for the per-quantity ledger.",
    "NOTE on the CONTRACTS \u00a713 G1a wording: the 6,592 figure for the blood_4h 1-50 band is a FULL-CSV (291,766-row) count and reproduces there exactly. The analytic-cohort (cohort_primary==1) 1-50 band is 5,832. Both are reported in logs/fix1_transfusion_audit.md; the contract's 'in the analytic cohort' phrasing names the wrong denominator.",
    "Informative-missingness: MISSING-vitals stratum mortality = 16.26% (v2 realized ~16.26%)."
  ]
